+# CHECK-UPDATE-ROOT — independent acceptance review
+
+Verdict: **BLOCK**. Reviewed 766cb9528 plus the three uncommitted updater files on 2026-09-11. No source fixes or repository commits. No compiler, llama executable, HTTP judge, benchmark, real bump, or scheduled-task changes were run. The compiler was stubbed in isolated temporary git fixtures; judge function probes stopped at the existing purity gate.
+
+## Findings
+
+1. **P1 — dirty source contents are not bound to the receipt.** `tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py:1256-1266` hashes `git status --porcelain`, HEAD and HEAD tree. Changing an already-modified `source.c` from v1 to v2 preserves all three values. Independent real-git probe printed `DIRTY_BYTES_CHANGED_IDENTITY_MATCHES True`. This also defeats the comment at lines 959-961 claiming a mid-build edit cannot be certified. Repair: bind the actual build-input content (or require a clean immutable candidate), compare before/after compilation, and reject changed input. Add dirty-to-different-dirty and edit-during-build tests.
+
+2. **P1 — a successful build can certify a different CMake source root.** `cmd_build:938-967` only checks cache existence; it never checks `CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY`. `parse_cache:829-848` drops INTERNAL entries, including that root. A fixture with `CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY:INTERNAL=C:/some/OTHER/checkout` reaches the compiler and writes the current repository's receipt on stubbed success. Configured build directories can also be absolute or traverse out of the checkout. Repair: canonicalize and verify the configured CMake source root against the named candidate and bind the actual build directory/configuration before compilation; reject mismatches before invoking CMake. A mere directory-name check is insufficient.
+
+3. **P1 — receipts certify no executable bytes and survive failed rebuilds.** `cmd_build:953-967` leaves an old receipt untouched on failure; `cmd_judge:986-1014` compares source metadata only. The receipt has exactly `build_dir, built_utc, dirty, head, status_sha256, tree`, with no artifact hashes. Independent probe replaced `llama-server.exe` after receipt creation and still reached the purity gate (`CHANGED_BINARY_REACHES_PURITY_GATE True`). A subsequent failing stubbed build returned 1 while the old receipt survived unchanged. A partially updated executable or manually replaced binary can therefore retain certification. Repair: invalidate the receipt before attempting a rebuild; atomically publish it only after successful input/output verification; record and verify the exact selected server executable and relevant runtime libraries/configuration. Test binary replacement and partial/failed rebuilds.
+
