+  claim is made that it is. Submodule contents are recorded as an opaque status entry, not walked.
+- **Artifact scope is the resolved binary's directory.** A runtime library that lives elsewhere on
+  the loader path is not hashed. Everything this build produces beside `llama-server` is.
+- **The suite takes ~6 minutes** now, up from ~3, because the bump tests do real replays. That is
+  the cost of not stubbing the identity under test.
+- **Pyright reports type diagnostics across this file**, almost all pre-existing: `git()` returns
+  `bytes | str` because of its `binary=` flag, so every string operation on its result is flagged.
+  Runtime behaviour is unaffected. I did not widen the change to add annotations.
+
+## Corrections to the brief and to the review
+
+The review is accurate on all six findings; I reproduced the reasoning for each and found no claim
+in it to refute. Two clarifications:
