+## 1. Finding 1 — the runbook command could write a row the next read rejects
+
+**The defect, reproduced before the fix.** With `user.email` unset, the R5 line
+`--recorded-by "$(git config user.email)"` still hands `replay-map` an argv token, and that token is
+the empty string. Run in Git-for-Windows bash through the same harness the new test uses, with
+`user.name` set and `USER`/`USERNAME`/`LOGNAME` popped:
