+```
+rc 0 slice ['--recorded-by', '', '--write'] identity-bytes 0
+```
+
+`--recorded-by` is `required=True`, so the parser is satisfied; `replay-map --write` records
+`"recorded_by": ""`; strict provenance then rejects the row as INCOMPLETE — after the rewrite, when
+the operator can no longer repair it. This matches the checker's own probe (`argc=3
+identity-bytes=0`).
