+## Finding 1 — the Bash ladder must pick the first candidate that is nonempty AND safe
+
+`UPDATE-RUNBOOK.md`, the `--recorded-by` `bash` fence. Before (R6): three rungs, each tested for
+NONEMPTY only, validated once after selection — so an unsafe `user.email` blocked a safe
+`user.name`, and an unsafe `USER` blocked a safe `USERNAME`. After (R7), the whole fence:
+
+```bash
+recorded_by=
+for candidate in "$(git config --get user.email)" "$(git config --get user.name)" \
+                 "${USER:-}" "${USERNAME:-}"; do
+    # Each candidate is tested on its OWN merits, before the next one is considered. `+` in the
+    # pattern cannot match an empty string, so this one test is both "nonempty" and "shell-safe":
+    # an UNSAFE user.email therefore falls through to a safe user.name rather than winning the
+    # ladder by being merely nonempty.
+    if printf '%s' "$candidate" | grep -Eq '^[A-Za-z0-9._@+ -]+$'; then
+        recorded_by="$candidate"
+        break
+    fi
+done
+if [ -z "$recorded_by" ]; then
+    echo 'REFUSE: no shell-safe identity for --recorded-by.' >&2
+    echo '        Set the identity you sign commits with, then re-run:' >&2
+    echo '            git config user.email your.real.address' >&2
+    exit 1
+fi
+python tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py protected-win replay-map --ref arifi/main \
+    --retained-ref arifi-pre-rebase --recorded-by "$recorded_by" --write
+```
+
+One regex test per candidate decides BOTH properties: `+` cannot match an empty string, so an empty
+candidate fails the same test an unsafe one fails, and the loop advances in either case. `USER` and
+`USERNAME` are now two separate rungs rather than one `${USER:-${USERNAME:-}}` expansion, which is
+what made an unsafe `USER` shadow a safe `USERNAME`.
