+## Finding 2 — `unknown-operator` is gone from output and from acceptance
+
+Removed: `RECORDED_BY_FALLBACK = "unknown-operator"`. `recorded_by_identity()` now returns `""` when
+nothing resolves. New single rule, used by the resolver, by `replay-map --write` and by every strict
+provenance read:
+
+```python
+_RECORDED_BY_PLACEHOLDER = re.compile(
+    r"^(unknown([ ._-]?operator)?|operator|someone|somebody|anonymous|nobody|none|n/?a|tbd|you|"
+    r"your[ ._-]?(name|address)|changeme|[^@]*@example\.(com|org|net|invalid))$", re.IGNORECASE)
+
+
+def recorded_by_problem(value: str) -> str:
+    """Why `value` is not an operator identity, or "" when it is one."""
+    v = (value or "").strip()
+    if not v:
+        return "empty"
+    if not _RECORDED_BY_SAFE.match(v):
+        return ("not shell-safe (%r carries characters that are metasyntax in a shell, or that "
+                "`shlex.split` eats)" % v)
+    if _RECORDED_BY_PLACEHOLDER.match(v):
+        return "a placeholder: %r names nobody, so it cannot make a registration statement" % v
+    return ""
+```
+
+Three enforcement points:
+
+| where | behaviour |
+|---|---|
+| `recorded_by_identity()` | each rung accepted only when `recorded_by_problem()` is empty; returns `""` at the end |
+| `cmd_protected_win_replay_map()` | `raise Loud(...)` BEFORE any work, so a placeholder never reaches disk |
+| `replay_provenance()` (strict read) | a row whose `recorded_by` is empty, unsafe or a placeholder contributes a problem and maps nothing |
