+  #    `--recorded-by` is a statement about a PERSON: it has no default. Set the
+  #    identity you sign commits with - `git config user.email` (or user.name) -
+  #    with your REAL address, then re-run the bump below: the complete sequence
+  #    then prints with the identity resolved into it, and a placeholder value
+  #    would be refused by replay-map and by every provenance read anyway.
+    python tools/arifi-sync/arifi_sync.py bump --onto <onto> --ref <ref>
+```
+
+Every INDENTED line remains a command runnable as printed, with no placeholder token and no `<`/`>`
+metasyntax, so the banner at `cmd_bump` ("no placeholder left to fill in") is true in BOTH branches.
+The ordinary branch is unchanged: a resolved literal identity, executed as printed by the
+convergence test through `shlex.split` + public `main`.
