+
+| What | How it is bound |
+|---|---|
+| Source, committed | `HEAD` sha and `HEAD^{tree}` sha |
+| Source, uncommitted | sha256 over the **bytes** of every modified, deleted or untracked path outside the build directory, plus the porcelain status listing |
+| CMake source root | `CMAKE_HOME_DIRECTORY` from the build cache, canonicalised, must equal the checkout |
+| Build directory | canonical absolute path, and it must be a strict subdirectory of the checkout holding no tracked files |
+| Recipe | every non-`INTERNAL`/non-`STATIC` entry of the `CMakeCache.txt` **under `build.build_dir`**, diffed against the committed snapshot; a LOST or CHANGED entry stops the build |
+| Build configuration | the literal string `Release` |
+| Judge binary | the selected candidate's relative path, plus its sha256 — including when it is extensionless |
+| Adjacent runtime set | sha256 of every `.exe`/`.dll`/`.so`/`.dylib` in the judge binary's own directory; replacement, removal, or the **addition of a library** all invalidate. An added unrelated executable does not — it is not on a loader path |
