+
+**Know what it preserves and what it writes before you run it.** `--draft` leaves your working-tree
+bytes, your index, your refs and your `git status` exactly as they were. It does **not** leave the
+repository untouched: it writes the snapshot's commit, tree and blob objects into `.git/objects`,
+and they stay there — unreachable, but present — until a `gc` that may never run. That is the whole
+reason it refuses untracked files (below), so read that paragraph before pointing it at a checkout
+with anything unusual lying in it.
